## Where I did not follow the reviewer

- Do not add a Gregorian year beside a Minguo year. a#26 and b#12 suggest «(۲۰۲۰)». That is a new number. R13 allows the ROC label and the Chinese gloss, and forbids the extra Gregorian digit. 109 and 112 stay once in running text; 民國109年 / 民國112年 sits in the gloss, which the checker collapses as a hanzi duplicate.
- Do not reformat «TWD 1.57M» (a#12). The test pins those bytes. «۱٫۵۷ میلیون دلار جدید تایوان» would fail that pin and would add a magnitude word the checker may multiply.
- Do not replace the Hangul `url:` (a#7). It is source metadata. The visible title is already Persian.
- Do not switch running numbers to Persian digits (a#23, b#14). R14’s fa style is comma thousands. Persian digits are allowed only if a whole file is consistent, and the reviewer’s ۱٬ grouping is not what the checker parses. Western comma-thousands were already consistent; I kept them. The formula’s asterisk and bare «TWD» were still rewritten.
- «من، ……،» is not the R15 placeholder. The forced letter now says «من، [نام]،».
- 009 did not get a prose rewrite. There is no first-person narrator and no comment-box line. The blank lines are the block structure the checker counts.
